      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69815,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 331,
        "headingId": 543,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T19:21:08"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 505,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 544,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69816,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 331,
        "headingId": 544,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Prostate gland, retrovesical space, retroperitoneum</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T19:21:08"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 506,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 545,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69817,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 331,
        "headingId": 545,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Patients may present with obstructive urinary symptoms, constipation, abdominal distention, and pain. Imaging studies often show large multiseptate masses involving the prostate gland and/or retrovesical space. Serum PSA is commonly elevated, and biopsies (if performed) are often non-diagnostic {26172350; 30808350}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T19:21:08"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 507,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 546,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69818,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 331,
        "headingId": 546,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>About 30&nbsp;cases have been reported in patients in their third to ninth decades of life {26172350; 30808350}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T19:21:08"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 508,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 547,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69819,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 331,
        "headingId": 547,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T19:21:08"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 509,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 548,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69820,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 331,
        "headingId": 548,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T19:21:08"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 516,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 555,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69821,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 331,
        "headingId": 555,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Cystadenomas may be intraprostatic, periprostatic but attached to the prostate by a pedicle, or entirely separate. Masses are large (70&ndash;450&nbsp;mm) and have smooth and/or bosselated outer surfaces. The cut aspect is multilocular, with cysts (usually &lt;&nbsp;20&nbsp;mm in diameter) separated by grey-white fibrous septa. The cysts often contain yellow or brown serous fluid and sometimes inspissated semi-solid material {1989460; 10604367; 16096417; 26900818}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T19:21:08"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 510,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 549,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69822,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 331,
        "headingId": 549,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Cysts are lined by a dual layer consisting of low columnar or atrophic secretory cells and flattened outer basal cells. Focal bland papillae may be seen. Cysts are surrounded by prostatic fibromuscular or fibrotic stroma, which may be hyalinized and show chronic inflammation. Squamous metaplasia may be seen in the lining epithelium {26900818}. No marked epithelial atypia is present. By immunohistochemistry, the lining epithelium stains for PSA, PAP, and other prostate lineage&ndash;specific markers. Basal cells are decorated with high-molecular-weight cytokeratin and p63 {1989460; 10604367; 16096417; 26900818}.</p>\r\n<p>Rarely, both high-grade prostatic intraepithelial neoplasia and acinar adenocarcinoma have been described as occurring in prostatic cystadenomas {12639673; 20518893}. Prostatic ductal adenocarcinoma can rarely present as a large multilocular mass resembling cystadenoma; however, prominent intracystic papillary growth and cytological atypia have been noted in cystadenocarcinoma {26900818}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T19:21:08"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 511,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 550,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69823,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 331,
        "headingId": 550,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Insufficient data</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T19:21:08"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 512,
