        "headingId": 551,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T19:21:08"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 515,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 554,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69825,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 331,
        "headingId": 554,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> a large multiloculated cystic mass in or around the prostate gland; cysts lined by bland prostatic secretory and basal cells; no marked cytological atypia; septa with fibromuscular or fibrous stroma.</p>\r\n<p><em>Desirable:</em> immunohistochemistry to confirm prostatic epithelial origin (if the differential diagnosis includes a seminal vesicle lesion).</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T19:21:08"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 513,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 552,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69826,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 331,
        "headingId": 552,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T19:21:08"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 514,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 553,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69827,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 331,
        "headingId": 553,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The therapy of choice is complete surgical excision, which may involve local resection, prostatectomy, or (rarely) pelvic exenteration {30808350}. Cases behave in a benign fashion; however, incomplete removal may result in tumour recurrence {1989460; 12438038; 30808350}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T19:21:08"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]